1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,880
Four payments. Zero interest. Nothing extra to pay.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,340
So who is paying for it?

3
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:07,720
Because somebody is.

4
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:10,560
And it might be you. Just not where you're looking.

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:16,060
Klarna does not lend you money.

6
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:20,490
It pays the shop. Today. In full.

7
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:22,390
Then you owe Klarna.

8
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:24,000
Hold onto that. It decides everything.

9
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:25,820
A ninety pound jacket.

10
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:27,790
Four payments of twenty-two fifty.

11
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:30,680
But the shop does not receive ninety.

12
00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:33,670
It receives about eighty-five.

13
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:35,060
Klarna keeps the rest.

14
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:39,400
Often three to six percent. Sometimes more.

15
00:00:39,790 --> 00:00:41,410
So where did that five pounds come from?

16
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:43,290
You paid ninety. The shop kept eighty-five.

17
00:00:44,410 --> 00:00:46,790
It was already inside the price.

18
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:50,820
And a shop does not absorb that fee.

19
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:54,200
It builds it into the sticker.

20
00:00:55,150 --> 00:00:57,190
The price goes up. For everyone.

21
00:00:57,770 --> 00:00:58,670
Including the man paying cash.

22
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:01,020
He has never used Klarna.

23
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:03,740
He is paying for it anyway.

24
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:06,300
Then there is being late.

25
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:09,860
Where late fees apply... that is revenue.

26
00:01:10,870 --> 00:01:12,330
A penalty that becomes their profit.

27
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:15,670
That is the oldest objection there is.

28
00:01:16,930 --> 00:01:18,080
And split a price into four...

29
00:01:18,690 --> 00:01:20,600
...and people spend more.

30
00:01:21,890 --> 00:01:25,600
That is not a side effect. That is the product.

31
00:01:26,860 --> 00:01:28,140
So is it halal?

32
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:31,760
Don't ask about the brand. Ask three questions.

33
00:01:32,210 --> 00:01:34,830
One. Is this a sale, or a loan?

34
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,630
Klarna paid the shop. You owe Klarna.

35
00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:39,610
That is a loan.

36
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:42,340
Two. Does anybody profit from that loan?

37
00:01:43,650 --> 00:01:46,240
Not from you. From the merchant's fee.

38
00:01:46,890 --> 00:01:50,340
A loan that brings a benefit to the lender.

39
00:01:51,090 --> 00:01:53,230
That is the exact phrase the scholars argue over.

40
00:01:54,690 --> 00:01:55,030
Three. Would cash have been cheaper?

41
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:57,890
If later costs more than now, you paid for time.

42
00:01:59,070 --> 00:02:00,730
Time is not a thing anyone can sell you.

43
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:01,980
And scholars genuinely differ here.

44
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:05,370
Same price as cash, no late fee, no interest...

45
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:06,260
...and many permit it.

46
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:09,330
Add a penalty, or a higher price for waiting...

47
00:02:10,220 --> 00:02:12,150
...and the disagreement ends.

48
00:02:12,690 --> 00:02:14,120
But here is the part nobody says.

49
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:16,780
Buy now, pay later is not the problem.

50
00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:18,740
Islam has had it for fourteen hundred years.

51
00:02:19,290 --> 00:02:20,770
It is called murabaha.

52
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:26,040
The seller buys the thing. Actually owns it.

53
00:02:26,490 --> 00:02:31,130
Then sells it to you at one disclosed price...

54
00:02:32,290 --> 00:02:35,360
...fixed at signing, paid over time.

55
00:02:36,310 --> 00:02:37,630
Late? You owe the same. Not a penny more.

56
00:02:38,370 --> 00:02:40,750
One price. One owner. No penalty.

57
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:44,070
"Pay later" was never the problem.

58
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:47,920
The problem is who earns on the "later".

59
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:52,950
Three questions. Ask them before you click.
